{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>במסה.</b> The name of a place mentioned above, \"and he called the name of place Massah.\" The bet is opened, like \"and Zebah and Zalmunna at Karkor,\" \"and he counted them by lambs\" — and I explained it there. The meaning is that they said, \"Is HaShem in our midst?\" And if He is, let Him serve us — only you have no need except to keep His commandments, and if you do what is good in His eyes, He will do all good to you and drive away all your enemies."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The Ibn Ezra supercommentary tradition reads this as a compressed argument: Israel tested HaShem by demanding proof of His presence and by treating Him as one who must perform for them. The clause ואם הוא נעבדנו is rendered hyper-literally, 'and if He is, let Him serve us,' preserving the abrupt terseness."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:40.013697334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}